      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَائِحٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of 1]. You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آفَةٌ جَائِحَةٌ</span>
<i>A destructive bane</i> or <i>pest</i> or <i>the like:</i> (Msb:)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَنَةٌ جَائِحَةٌ</span> <i>a year of drought</i> or <i>dearth</i> or
<i>sterility:</i> (Mgh:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَوَائِحُ</span>. (Mgh, Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
[And hence,] The <i>locust.</i> (IAar, T in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جحى</span>.)

